# Meeting Summary - Target State Architecture Discussion

**Date:** 2026-08-28
**Participants:** Person A (Chief Data Officer, MNC Pvt Ltd; Client Sponsor); Person B (Head of BI & Reporting, MNC Pvt Ltd); Person C (Head of IT Infrastructure, MNC Pvt Ltd); Person D (Enterprise Architect, Delivery Team); Person E (Platform Engineering Lead, Delivery Team)
**Purpose:** Narrow the target-state platform and cloud direction so the delivery team can begin scoping the landing zone, and identify initial requirements and recommendation work.

## Executive summary
MNC Pvt Ltd stated a strong direction toward Azure because of its Microsoft estate, existing Enterprise Agreement, Entra ID, Office 365, and Power BI usage. The analytics compute decision remains open between Microsoft Fabric and Azure Databricks; business familiarity, speed, and manageability favor guided managed tooling, while flexibility and an open lakehouse favor Databricks. Azure Data Lake Storage Gen2 was recommended as a compute-independent storage foundation, with Azure Data Factory as the default for batch and hourly ingestion. The first target-state use case should be Supply Chain inventory visibility, delivered in parallel with the existing mart within the current quarter. A shared semantic layer and Finance-visible cost tracking from week one were identified as hard requirements. The date needs confirmation because the transcript header says 2026-09-03 while the supplied meeting context and summary filename identify 2026-08-28.

